  "result": "The file is `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`. Messages queued for a customer's receiving server are webhook deliveries, and this file holds both settings:\n\n- **How many attempts are allowed:** `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` (line 22). Once a delivery's `attempts` count is above this, `runWebhookDeliveryJob` marks it failed with \"giving up after N attempts\" (lines 49–56).\n- **How the wait grows:** `backoffMs(attempts)` (lines 90–93) doubles the wait each time: 1s, 2s, 4s and so on, capped at five minutes (`300_000` ms). A delivery with no prior attempts is retried straight away.\n\nThree similar-looking places don't control this:\n- `src/config/constants.ts` defines `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5`, but no code uses it.\n- `src/server/jobs/queue.ts` has its own `MAX_ATTEMPTS` and `backoffMs`, but those apply to the general in-process job queue, not webhook deliveries.\n- `src/app/api/cron/webhook-delivery/route.ts` only triggers `runWebhookDeliveryJob`.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
